  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/AAC4A7">Proposition <span data-tag="AAC4A7">4.2.4.4</span>.</a>straightening of diagrams Let $S$ be a small simplicial set, $\calC $ a small simplicial category, and $u: \sCoNerve [S] \rightarrow \calC $ an equivalence. Suppose that $\mathbf{A}$ is a combinatorial simplicial model category, and let $\calU $ be a $\calC $-chunk of $\mathbf{A}$ (see Definition <a href="/tag/" data-tag="">None</a>). Then the induced map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \sNerve ( \calU ^{\calC } )^{\circ } \rightarrow \Fun (S, \sNerve (\calU ^{\circ }) ) \]
</div>
  <p> is a categorical equivalence of simplicial sets. </p>
